  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1) REST XML output serialization is via org.fcrepo.server.rest.DefaultSerializer",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) REST Serialization to HTML is (1) plus an xslt, in the individual handlers for the rest methods",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "3) See ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-886#icft=FCREPO-886"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": " - there is additional serialization in the default disseminators",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We should consider the serialization as independent from the API, and move the serialization code (and possibly refactor) into (perhaps) org.fcrepo.server.storage.types.serializers - as it seems that it is classes in org.fcrepo.server.storage.types that require serialization.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This should be refactored to include the to-HTML serialization.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This could form the basis of a standard serialization package able to handle a variety of formats, HTML, XML, text, JSON, etc etc.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "org.fcrepo.server.access.defaultdisseminator.ObjectInfoAsXML() should be removed; and the code scanned for any other serialization that should be refactored into the new serialization package.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
